            {
              "name": "messages",
              "value": "={{ \n  JSON.stringify([{\n    \"role\": \"user\",\n    \"content\": `CRITICAL INSTRUCTION: You are an API endpoint acting as an expert instructional designer. You must output ONLY a raw, valid JSON array. Do not include markdown formatting, backticks, or any conversational text. ALWAYS OUTPUT IN ENGLISH.\n\nExpand the requested lesson into AT LEAST 3 parts and NO MORE THAN 5 parts. \nTo maximize Germane Cognitive Load, strictly follow this progression for your generated parts:\n- Part 1: Introduce the core concept and provide a simple mental model or analogy.\n- Part 2 & 3: Provide clear examples, and at least one \"non-example\" (what the concept is NOT).\n- Part 4 & 5 (Optional): Provide an application, knowledge check, or advanced edge-case.\n\nExample Input:\nMAIN OBJECTIVE: \"Teach basic math\"\nCOURSE OUTLINE: \"1. Addition\"\nDATA FROM RAG: \"1+1=2\"\n\nExample Output:\n[\n  {\n    \"slide_title\": \"the topic of the slide\",\n    \"main_content\": \"Addition is the process of bringing two or more numbers together to make a new total.\",\n    \"objective\": \"Understand the concept of addition.\"\n  }\n]\n\nThis is ONLY FOR CONTEXT:\nMAIN OBJECTIVE: ${JSON.stringify($json.slide)}\nCOURSE OUTLINE: ${JSON.stringify($json.outline)}\nDATA FROM RAG: ${JSON.stringify($json.rag_data)}\n\nExpand ONLY the following lesson to generate slides to teach users. Keep main_content concise to minimize extraneous load:  ${JSON.stringify($json.lesson)}`\n  }]) \n}}"
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {}
      },
